# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtualenv and bytecode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The fine-tuned model — 418MB, four times GitHub's 100MB per-file limit.
#
# Regenerable: `train.py --epochs 6 --class-weights` rebuilds it from
# data/labeled-all.jsonl in about four hours on CPU. The labels are what
# actually cost money; the weights are just a slow function of them.
#
# To distribute it, attach bundle/document-kind-classifier.tar.gz to a GitHub
# Release (2GB asset limit, and release assets do not bloat clones) rather
# than committing it or paying for LFS bandwidth on every clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
model/
bundle/
*.tar.gz
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded label files: 298MB between them, because each row carries a full
# copy of document text that already lives in the legal-ai-mvp corpus.
#
# data/labeled-all.jsonl supersedes all three — same labels, no inlined text,
# 1.8MB — and dataset.py reads document text from the corpus on demand. It is
# committed deliberately: regenerating those labels means re-running the
# DeepSeek pass, which is the one step that costs real money.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/labeled.jsonl
data/labeled.round1.jsonl
data/labeled.v1.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run logs and scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
out/*.log
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit credentials. This project reads DEEPSEEK_API_KEY from the
# legal-ai-mvp checkout's .env at runtime and never copies it here — this
# entry exists so that stays true.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
